  "title": "India's GST Reforms and ITC Expansion",
  "summary": "India's GST reforms aim to expand input tax credit (ITC) coverage for businesses across sectors, including motor vehicles and energy, while addressing tax disparities and encouraging wider coverage. The reforms include provisions for group health and life insurance, with potential tax benefits for electric vehicles.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "India's GST reforms aim to expand input tax credit (ITC) coverage for businesses across sectors, including motor vehicles and energy, while addressing tax disparities and encouraging wider coverage.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reforms include provisions for group health and life insurance, with potential tax benefits for electric vehicles.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The GST Council is likely to consider sweeping process reforms to decriminalise GST offences, remove arrest powers of GST officers and make tax compliance easier for businesses, including e-commerce suppliers.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
