      "title": "GST Council meeting rescheduled again, to take place on October 8",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/finance/news/57th-gst-council-meeting-rescheduled-to-october-8-for-second-time-126100501256_1.html",
      "description": "The 57th GST Council meeting has been rescheduled for the second time, and the new date is October 8.\nIn an office memorandum, the GST Council Secretariat said that the meeting is being rescheduled due to \"unavoidable circumstances\".\nThe Council meeting was scheduled to be held on October 7.\nThe GST Council, chaired by Union Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman and comprising state ministers, will, in its meeting on Thursday, discuss changes in registration, returns, and refunds mechanism.\nIt would also discuss policy reforms to resolve GST disputes and improve the flow of input tax credit, with the aim of reducing the time and cost of compliance.\nAccording to sources, the GST Council is likely to consider sweeping process reforms to decriminalise GST offences, remove arrest powers of GST officers and make tax compliance easier for businesses, including e-commerce suppliers.\nThis is the second time that the date of the 57th GST Council meeting has been rescheduled.\nThe meeting, w",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-06T04:25:11"
    }
